.TH PDF-TOOLS 1 2026-10-30 "PDF Tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pdf-tools \- view, redact, fill, annotate, sign, OCR, compare, crop and merge PDF files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdf-tools
.RB [ \-\-new\-window ]
.RI [ file.pdf " ...]"
.br
.B pdf-tools \-\-forward
.I file.pdf line source.tex
.br
.B pdf-tools
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.I input.pdf
.br
.B pdf-tools help
|
.B \-\-help
|
.B \-\-install\-desktop
|
.B \-\-uninstall\-desktop
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pdf-tools
opens PDF files in a window with one tab per document.
Edits stay in the window until you save, and every edit can be undone.
.PP
Redaction removes the text, images and drawings under each box from the file;
it does not just paint over them.
A file saved with redactions or crops also loses its hidden data: metadata,
attachments, scripts, hidden text (such as the invisible text layer of a
scanned document) and embedded thumbnails.
After saving, the status line says whether any text was still found under a
redaction.
.PP
All windows belong to one running program.
Opening more files, from a terminal or the application launcher, adds tabs to
the window you used last (a file that is already open is shown where it is);
.B \-\-new\-window
opens them in a new window instead.
.B File > New window
opens another window, and a tab's right-click menu moves it, with its unsaved
edits and undo history, to a window of its own.
When the tabs do not fit, the tab strip scrolls (mouse wheel or its thin
scrollbar); the search button at its end lists the open tabs, filtered as you
type.
.PP
The same operations are also available as commands that run without the window
(see
.BR COMMANDS ).
.SH THE WINDOW
.SS Tools
.TP
.BR View " (V)"
Read the document, fill form fields, drag to select text (Alt+drag selects a
rectangle) and right-click the selection to copy, mark or redact it.
.TP
.BR Redact " (R)"
Drag over text to redact it, or draw a free rectangle with Alt+drag or with
.B Snap to text
turned off.
.B Auto fill
paints each box in the colour around it.
.B Find personal data
lists e-mail addresses, phone numbers, IBANs, card numbers, dates and ID numbers
on all pages; tick what to mark for redaction.
.TP
.BR Highlight " (H)"
Drag over text to mark it: highlight, underline, strikethrough, squiggly line or
text colour, with an optional comment.
.TP
.BR Note " (N)"
Click to add a sticky note.
.TP
.BR Text " (T)"
Click and type on the page, or drag first to set a width and the text wraps
inside it.
The bar above the box sets the font, size, bold, italic and colour.
Esc or clicking elsewhere finishes; double-click a box to edit it again.
.TP
.BR Sign " (S)"
Click to place a saved signature, or draw or import a new one.
.B Sign with certificate
places a box for a digital signature with a PKCS#12 certificate (.p12, .pfx);
the document is signed when you save, after asking for the certificate's
password, which is never stored.
.TP
.BR Image " (I)"
Click, or drag a box, to place a picture (PNG, JPEG, WebP and other common
formats) in full colour; drag it or its corner to move or resize it.
.TP
.BR Draw " (D)"
Draw freehand with a pen colour, width and style: pen, highlighter (wide and
see-through, multiplied over the page), marker (thicker, slightly see-through) or
dashed; the style is remembered as
.BR pen_style .
Strokes made in quick succession form one drawing, saved as a PDF ink
annotation that other viewers show and can remove.
.TP
.BR Shape " (O)"
Drag a rectangle, ellipse, line or arrow, saved as a PDF annotation.
.TP
.BR Crop " (C)"
Drag a rectangle, then crop this page, all pages or the ticked pages to it, or
crop the page to its content.
The area outside is dimmed while you work and removed when you save.
.SS Pages
The
.B Pages
sidebar shows a thumbnail per page.
Drag thumbnails to reorder pages, tick pages to act on several at once, and
right-click for rotate, crop to content, insert pages from another PDF and
remove; the same commands are in the Pages menu and in the right-click menu
of the page itself.
Right-clicking a placed edit (text box, mark, note, redaction, signature, image,
drawing, crop)
or one of the document's own annotations offers its own commands, such as
edit, comment, style, colour and delete.
The
.B Edits
tab lists every unsaved change by page; hover over one and click its X to drop
just that change.
The
.B Annotations
tab lists the notes and marks in the document.
The
.B Outline
tab shows the bookmarks; add, rename, delete and drag them to reorder or nest.
.SS More tools
.TP
.B Bates numbering
Stamps PREFIX000001SUFFIX on a corner of each (ticked) page.
.TP
.B Watermark
Stamps text diagonally across, in the centre or on a corner of the pages, with
an opacity.
.TP
.B Recognize text (OCR)
Runs Tesseract on scanned pages and opens a copy with an invisible, searchable
text layer.
The language data
.RI ( lang .traineddata)
is looked up in
.BR $TESSDATA_PREFIX ,
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/pdf-tools/tessdata ,
next to the program and in the system's data folders.
.TP
.B Compare with...
Opens a tab with two PDFs side by side and the words that differ marked on each.
.TP
.B Document properties
Edits the title, author, subject and keywords.
.SS View
Fit width (Ctrl+0) or fit height (Ctrl+9), continuous or single pages, two
pages side by side (optionally with the cover alone), and presentation mode
(F5: full screen, one page, arrows or clicks to step, Esc to leave).
The accent colour can be chosen per theme under
.BR "View > Appearance" .
.SS Saving
.B Save
replaces the file and moves the original to the trash.
.B Save As
writes a copy,
.B Export pages
writes a copy of some pages (optionally flattened to images),
.B Export pages as images
saves PNG or JPEG files, and
.B Protect with password
writes an AES-256 encrypted copy.
A password protected file asks for its password when opened and keeps it when
saved.
.SS Combine & split
One tab (on Home, Ctrl+M, or
.B Split into files
for the open document) combines, splits and extracts.
Add one or more PDFs or images (each image becomes a page): all their pages
appear in one grid, each file marked by its own colour.
Drag pages to reorder them, select and press Delete to drop them, and click the
strip left of a page to start a new file there (or cut every N pages).
Without cuts, Save writes one combined file; with cuts, one file per part,
whose names can be edited.
.SS Keyboard
.TS
l l.
Ctrl+O	open files
Ctrl+S	save
Ctrl+Shift+S	save as
Ctrl+E	export pages
Ctrl+P	print
Ctrl+Z	undo
Ctrl+Shift+Z, Ctrl+Y	redo
Ctrl+F	find; Enter and Shift+Enter step
Ctrl+C	copy the selected text
Delete	remove the selected edit or pages
Ctrl++, Ctrl+\-	zoom in, zoom out
Ctrl+0	fit the width
Ctrl+9	fit the height
F5	presentation
Left, PgUp	previous page
Right, PgDn	next page
Ctrl+Shift+L, Ctrl+Shift+R	rotate left, right
F9	show or hide the sidebar
Ctrl+M	combine and split PDFs
Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+Tab	next, previous tab
Ctrl+W	close the tab
Ctrl+N	new window
Ctrl+Shift+W	close the window
Ctrl+Q	quit (all windows)
Ctrl+click	open the TeX source line
.TE
.SH LATEX
An open PDF reloads by itself whenever the file changes on disk, keeping the
page, zoom and scroll position, so a running
.B latexmk \-pvc
shows every build.
If the tab has unsaved edits, you are asked first.
.PP
Compile with
.B \-synctex=1
to link the PDF and its sources:
.TP
.B Ctrl+click
in the PDF opens the source line that produced that spot.
The editor command is asked for on first use and stored as
.B editor_command
in the settings file;
.B %f
is replaced by the file and
.B %l
by the line, for example
.BR "code \-g %f:%l" .
.TP
.BI "pdf-tools \-\-forward " "file.pdf line source.tex"
shows where a source line is typeset: the window showing that PDF (or the one
used last) jumps there and briefly highlights it.
Configure your editor to run this command for its "view in PDF" action.
.SH COMMANDS
These run without the window, never ask questions, and print one JSON object.
Pages are numbered from 1; ranges look like
.BR 1\-3,7 ;
positions are PDF points (1/72 inch) from the top-left corner of the page.
Output files must differ from the input.
An encrypted input needs
.BI \-\-password " pw"
and the output keeps that password.
Run
.BI "pdf-tools " command " \-\-help"
for the full option list of a command.
.TP
.BI "info " input.pdf
Page count and sizes, fonts, form fields with their values, annotations,
metadata, whether the file is encrypted and whether SyncTeX data exists.
.TP
.BI "redact " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf"
Redact every match of
.BI \-\-text " string"
and
.BI \-\-regex " pattern"
(both repeatable; text matches ignore case unless
.BR \-\-case\-sensitive ).
.BI \-\-pages " ranges"
limits the pages,
.BI \-\-fill " #rrggbb"
sets the box colour (default black).
The output lists every match and any text still found under a box.
.TP
.BI "fill " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf " \-\-field " name=value"
Fill form fields (repeatable); checkboxes take
.B true
or
.BR false .
Field names are listed by
.BR info .
.TP
.BI "pages " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf"
.BI \-\-order " 3,1,2"
sets the page order (ranges may count down, as in
.BR 5\-1 ;
pages left out are dropped),
.BI \-\-remove " ranges"
removes pages,
.BI \-\-rotate " page:degrees"
rotates by a multiple of 90,
.BI \-\-crop " page:x0,y0,x1,y1"
crops to a box, and
.BR \-\-crop\-content " [\fIranges\fR]"
crops pages to their content.
Content outside a crop is deleted.
.TP
.BI "merge " "a.pdf b.pdf:1-3 photo.jpg ... " \-o " output.pdf"
Join PDFs, each optionally limited to some pages, and images, each of which
becomes a page.
.TP
.BI "split " "input.pdf " "\-\-every " n " \-d " folder
.TQ
.BI "split " "input.pdf " "\-\-at " pages " \-d " folder
Write
.IR name \-part1.pdf ", " name \-part2.pdf ", ..."
with
.I n
pages each, or starting a new part at each listed page.
.TP
.BI "protect " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf " \-\-password " new"
Write an AES-256 encrypted copy
.RB ( \-\-current\-password
for an input that already has one).
.TP
.BI "unprotect " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf " \-\-password " current"
Write a copy without the password.
.TP
.BI "flatten " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf"
Turn every page into an image
.RB ( \-\-dpi ,
default 200), so no text, layers or hidden content remain.
.TP
.BI "synctex " "input.pdf " "\-\-page " n " \-\-at " x,y
Print the source file and line typeset at that point.
.TP
.BI "synctex " "input.pdf " "\-\-source " file.tex " \-\-line " n
Print the page and boxes where that source line is typeset.
.TP
.BI "search " input.pdf " \-\-text " string
Print the pages and boxes of each match
.RB ( \-\-pages ,
.BR \-\-case\-sensitive ).
.TP
.BI "inspect " input.pdf
List annotations, with their index on each page, and form fields.
.TP
.BI "render " "input.pdf " \-o " page.png"
Render one page
.RB ( \-\-page ,
.BR \-\-dpi ).
.TP
.BI "export\-images " "input.pdf " \-d " folder"
Save pages as
.IR name \-page N .png
.RB ( \-\-pages ,
.BR \-\-format " png|jpeg,"
.BR \-\-dpi ).
.TP
.BI "ocr " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf"
Add an invisible, searchable text layer to scanned pages with Tesseract
.RB ( \-\-pages ,
.BI \-\-language " deu+eng" ,
.BI \-\-tessdata " folder" ).
.TP
.BI "compare " "a.pdf b.pdf"
Print, per page, the boxes of words only in the first and only in the second
file
.RB ( \-\-password2
for the second).
.TP
.BI "bates " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf"
Stamp Bates numbers
.RB ( \-\-prefix ,
.BR \-\-suffix ,
.BR \-\-start ,
.BR \-\-digits ,
.BR \-\-position ,
.BR \-\-size ,
.BR \-\-pages ,
.BR \-\-color ).
.TP
.BI "watermark " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf " \-\-text " text"
Stamp text diagonally or at a position
.RB ( \-\-position ,
.BR \-\-size ,
.BR \-\-opacity ,
.BR \-\-pages ,
.BR \-\-color ).
.TP
.BI "annotate " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf " \-\-page " n " \-\-type " type " \-\-rect " x0,y0,x1,y1"
Add a highlight, underline, strikeout, squiggly or text-colour mark, or a note
.RB ( \-\-text ,
.BR \-\-color ).
.TP
.BI "draw " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf " \-\-page " n " \-\-points " x,y;x,y;..."
Add a freehand ink drawing
.RB ( \-\-width ,
.BR \-\-color ,
.BR \-\-style " pen|highlighter|marker|dashed" ).
.TP
.BI "insert\-text " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf " \-\-page " n " \-\-at " x,y " \-\-text " text"
Write text into the page
.RB ( \-\-size ,
.BR \-\-font ,
.BR \-\-width ,
.BR \-\-color ).
.TP
.BI "insert\-image " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf " \-\-page " n " \-\-image " file " \-\-rect " box"
Place a picture, keeping its proportions.
.TP
.BI "sign " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf " \-\-page " n " \-\-rect " box"
With
.BI \-\-image " file"
place a signature picture; with
.BI \-\-cert " file.p12"
and
.B \-\-cert\-password
sign digitally (PKCS#7, incremental save;
.B \-\-reason
is shown with the signature).
.TP
.BI "scrub " "input.pdf " \-o " output.pdf"
Remove metadata, attachments, scripts, hidden text and thumbnails.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage summary.
.TP
.B help
Print the guide for scripts and agents (AGENTS.md).
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open the given files (or Home) in a new window rather than the one used last.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-desktop
Add PDF Tools to the application launcher and install its icon, for the current
user.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall\-desktop
Remove them again.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 1
Error; the JSON output has an
.B error
message.
.TP
.B 2
.B redact
wrote the file, but text was still found under a redaction.
.TP
.B 3
Nothing matched; nothing was written.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pdf-tools/settings.toml
Settings, with a comment for each; edit while the program is closed.
.TP
.I ~/.config/pdf-tools/signatures/
Saved signatures.
.TP
.IB name .synctex.gz
SyncTeX data written by TeX next to
.IR name .pdf.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/pdf-tools/tessdata/
Tesseract language data for OCR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PDF_TOOLS_LOG
Log level:
.BR error ", " warn " (default), " info " or " debug .
.TP
.B TESSDATA_PREFIX
Folder with Tesseract language data.
.SH EXAMPLES
Remove a name and every IBAN from a statement:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pdf-tools redact statement.pdf \-o statement\-redacted.pdf \e
    \-\-text "Jane Doe" \-\-regex 'DE\ed{20}'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Keep pages 1 to 3 of a scan, turned upright and trimmed to their content:
.PP
.RS
.nf
pdf-tools pages scan.pdf \-o trimmed.pdf \-\-order 1\-3 \e
    \-\-rotate 1:90 \-\-rotate 2:90 \-\-rotate 3:90 \-\-crop\-content
.fi
.RE
.PP
Write a LaTeX document with live preview:
.PP
.RS
.nf
latexmk \-pdf \-pvc \-synctex=1 paper.tex &
pdf-tools paper.pdf
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR latexmk (1),
.BR synctex (1),
.BR qpdf (1)
.PP
